  "raw_text": "257\n\nAiya tiwan\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nI forget\n \n/ olvido\n\nAmya tiwan\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nyou forget\n \n/ olvidas\n\nLap tiwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nLap-tiwaia\n-dict\n;\n \nLaptiwaia\n-sp\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nLap tikaia)\n \n–\n \nto be lost suddenly, to vanish, to\ndisappear\n \n/ perderse de repente, desaparecer\n\nLus tiwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nLus tikaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto lose\n \n/ perder\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh50\n):\n \nLus tiwan ba kli briaia dukiara, ...\n \n–\n \nIn order to have again what was lost...\n \n/ Para tener de nuevo lo que se\nperdió...)\n\nPlun tiwan\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfamine, food shortage\n \n/ hambre, escasez de alimentos\n\nPrui tiwaia\n \n(\nkt\n,\nbh\n,\nfy\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto lose in death\n \n/ perder en la muerte\n\nTanis tiwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be lost, to perish\n \n/ estar perdido, perecer Is foolishness implied? Used in Jan 3:16 in place of\n\ndestroyed\n\nTiwan\n \n–\n \nlost\n \n/ perdido, perdió\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-06/20\n):\n \nJehova nahki ai dara walisa sîp kum tiwan ba kli tawi balisa taim?\n \n–\n \nHow does Jehovah feel when a\nlost sheep returns?\n \n/ ¿Cómo se siente Jehová cuando regresa una oveja perdida?)\n\nTiwi auya kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be forgetting\n \n/ estar olvidando\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-01/21\n):\n \nDîa ba wan marikisa naiwa piua ra latwan lâka ba tiwi auya sa?\n \n–\n \nWhat shows us that love is being\nforgotten about today?\n \n/ ¿Qué nos muestra que el amor se está olvidando hoy?)\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nbackside, buttocks\n \n/ trasero, nalgas\n\n(Construct:\n \nTnaita\n \n–\n \nmy backside\n \n/ mi trasero;\n \nTnamta\n \n–\n \nyour backside\n \n/ tu trasero;\n \nAi tnata\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their backside\n \n/ su\ntrasero)\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata\n,\n \nPnata\n) (adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \nfinal, last, end, conclusion, ending, result, goal, objective\n \n/ final, último, conclusión,\nresultado, objetivo\n\n(Construct:\n \nTnatki\n \n–\n \nmy ending\n \n/ mi final;\n \nTnatkam\n \n–\n \nyour ending\n \n/ tu final;\n \nTnatka\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their ending\n \n/ su final)\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata\n,\n \nPnata\n)\n \naimakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto completely accomplish, to fulfill, to come to an accomplished end\n \n/\nlograr completamente, cumplir, llegar a un fin logrado\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh92\n):\n \nNaha tnata aimaki ba diara kum tara sa\n \n–\n \nThe fulfilling of this is a big thing\n \n/ El cumplimiento de esto es una\n\ngran cosa\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nYawan nahki nu sa Baibil pramiska nani ba tnata aimakbia ba?\n \n–\n \nHow do we know that the Bible promises will be\n\nfulfilled?\n \n/ ¿Cómo sabemos que las promesas bíblicas se cumplirán?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n11/20\n):\n \nG\nȃ\nd tintka watla paskaia warkka tnata aimakan taim, Moses mita warkka ba laki kaikan.\n \n–\n \nWhen the\n\nwork to make God’s tabernacle was completed, the work was\n \nexamined by Moses.\n \n/\n \nCuando se completó la obra para\n\nhacer el tabernáculo de Dios,\n \nel trabajo fue examinado por Moisés.\n)\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nalkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto come to a finish, to finish, to conclude, to reach an end, to reach a\n\nconclusion, to reach a goal, to accomplish an objective\n \n/ llegar a un final, terminar, concluir, llegar a una\n\nconclusión, alcanzar una meta, lograr un objetivo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/20\n):\n \nYawan diaura lukaia sa, bara nahki tnata alkaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nOn what thing are we to think (focus) upon,\nand how are we able to reach the end (goal)?\n \n/\n \n¿En qué debemos pensar (centrarnos) y cómo podemos alcanzar el fin\n(meta)?)\n\nTnata\n \n(\na/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nba\n \n–\n \nthe end\n \n/ el fin\n\n(Construct:\n \nTnatka (a/t: Natka\n,\n \nPnatka) ba\n)\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata\n,\n \nPnata\n)\n \nkat\n \n–\n \nin the end, at the end, finally, to the end, until the end\n \n/ al final, finalmente, hasta\nel final\n\nTâ wina tnata kat\n \n–\n \nfrom beginning to end\n \n/ de principio a fin\n\nTnata kat daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto do until the end, to do until completion\n \n/ hacer hasta el final, hacer hasta la\nfinalización\n\nAlki tnata kat daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto put in practice until the end, to apply until completion\n \n/ poner en\npráctica hasta el final, aplicar hasta completar\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nkrikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto begin, to commence\n \n/ comenzar\n\nTnata\n \n(\na/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nlukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto imitate, to mock\n \n/ imitar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n01/21\n):\n \nNasariu nani ra yawan nahki tnata lukaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nHow can we imitate the Nazirites?\n \n/ Cómo\n\npodemos imitar a los\n \nnazareos?)\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nmangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto terminate, to bring to an end, to accompany in music\n \n/ terminar,\nponer fin, acompañar en la música\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nprakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto conclude, to finish\n \n/ concluir, terminar",
